{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nFive residues in the plan-review attestation stack, each confirmed by both semantic reference search and string grep. All cites re-measured on origin/main `38f8587f65d`.\n\n**1. Dead kwarg.** `manifest.py:289 _hash_basis(repo_root=None, *, at_current_gate_ref=False)`. No src caller passes it (`code_review/region_gate.py:62`, `code_review/sidecar.py:258`, `plan_review/attest.py:226`, `manifest.py:440`, `workflow/plan_review_recovery.py:193` — all under `src/rebar/llm/`). Its branch `:302-303` delegates to `gate_ref_hash_basis` (`manifest.py:240`), which is independently reachable and stays. Only `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_ref_coherence.py:171,176,181,218` pass it. `docs/adr/0002-code-drift-invalidation.md:119` records the signature.\n\n**2. Unconsumed function.** `read_set.py:189-214 terraform_membership_entries`, plus its comment/constant `:185-186 _TERRAFORM_GLOB_SUFFIXES` — no src caller; only `tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py:223-231`. ADR 0115 `:86-87` defers remote module *content*, not membership globs, so nothing awaits it; under ADR 0111 code waiting for a consumer is deleted.\n\n**3. Behaviourless enum member.** `pin_health.py:15 PlanValidityProfile` is read in exactly one place, `attest.py:665 if profile is PlanValidityProfile.DEFAULT`, so `CLOSE` and `DRIFT_REFRESH` (`pin_health.py:18`) are identical; nothing serialises `.value`/`.name`. `tests/unit/test_attestation_invalidation.py:262-291` exists only to assert that equivalence.\n\n**4. Duplicated message.** `attest.py:426` and `:466` render a byte-identical \"… could not be resolved to a snapshot, so the attestation cannot …\" from two arms.\n\n**5. Status enum misaligned with the wire in BOTH directions.** `src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_status.schema.json:11` declares `not-closed`, which `compute_validity` emits only under `kind == \"completion-verifier\"` (`attest.py:622-628`); `tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py:23,54` already documents and asserts its exclusion from the plan-review vocabulary. Conversely `attest_gate.py:159` passes `verify_signature`'s verdict through verbatim, and 6 of the 7 failure verdicts are declared *deliberately* — the enum's own description calls them \"the signature-check verdicts a non-certified attestation can carry\". The 7th, `key_not_valid_at_era` (`types.py:379-389`, produced at `attest/opcert.py:308,330`), is absent: the one genuine leak, observed by `tests/unit/test_opcert_cross_environment_c21f.py:225`. The pass-through is contract, not accident — `test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py:63,65` assert the signature verdicts stay out of the blocking bucket and bucket as `infra` (fail-open). So declare the missing member rather than suppress the class. Neither `_mcp_models.py` nor `types.py` declares a `PlanReviewStatus` mirror, so the schema is the sole enum declaration and no other typed surface changes.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. **`manifest.py`** — delete the `:302-303` branch and the kwarg's docstring text (`:294` plus the mode bullet); signature becomes `def _hash_basis(repo_root=None) -> str`. Strip the kwarg's name from `gate_ref_hash_basis`'s docstring at `:244`.\n2. **`read_set.py`** — delete `:185-186` and `:189-214`.\n3. **`pin_health.py`** — delete `DRIFT_REFRESH` (`:18`). `attest.py:244` becomes `profile=PlanValidityProfile.CLOSE` with the comment \"CLOSE = skip code-freshness (the only non-DEFAULT behaviour)\"; reword the `attest.py:534` comment that names `DEFAULT/DRIFT_REFRESH`. Unchanged (all name DEFAULT or CLOSE): `_commands/gates.py:229`, `attest_gate.py:172`, `code_review/bugfix_size_gate.py:232`, `docs/plan-review-gate.md:1099`. `attest.drift_refresh_candidate` keeps its name — only the member it passes changes.\n4. **`attest.py`** — add `_unresolvable_ref_reason(ref: str | None) -> str` (`named = f\"'{ref}'\" if ref else \"the configured gate ref\"`); `:426` and `:466` each return it.\n5. **Align the enum, leaving the `attest_gate.py:159` pass-through UNCHANGED** — in the schema `:11` drop `not-closed`, add `key_not_valid_at_era`, and update \"The last 6 values (…)\" to name all 7. Mirror in the prose that restates the vocabulary: `attest_gate.py:203` (drop) and `:208` (add); `_mcp_reads.py:37` (drop) and `:40` (add). `llm/gate_runs.py:379` is the completion-verifier surface where `not-closed` IS reachable — leave it.\n6. **`docs/adr/0002-code-drift-invalidation.md:119`** — amend the recorded signature to `_hash_basis(repo_root)` and append an amendment note in the file's existing \"*(amended by …)*\" style, naming this story and pointing the gate-ref mode at `gate_ref_hash_basis`. It must not retain the kwarg's name; AC1 greps `docs`.\n7. **`docs/release-notes.md`** — one entry: the enum is realigned with what the surface emits (`not-closed` out, `key_not_valid_at_era` in); backward-compatible under `docs/api-stability.md:23` — no required key removed or retyped, and the emitted set is now a subset of the declared enum.\n\n## Scope\n\nOut of scope: `_legacy_material_ok` (`attest.py:727`, callers `:71,634,687`, corpus contract `llm/evals/plan_replay/corpus.py:10,39`); the delta explainers; `compute_validity`'s completion arm. `tests/fixtures/cloud_adf_corpus/bodies_00.json` and `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_corpus/code_arrow.json` quote `at_current_gate_ref` inside frozen archived report bodies — immutable corpus data, which is why AC1 carries `':!tests/fixtures'` instead of failing against them.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `test_ref_coherence.py:171,176,181,218` → `manifest.gate_ref_hash_basis(str(repo)).path`; assertions unchanged. Reword the comments at `:167,174,178` that name the kwarg (AC1 greps `tests`).\n- Delete `test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py:223-231`.\n- `test_attestation_invalidation.py:262-291` asserts `close[\"valid\"] is refresh[\"valid\"] is True` and `close[\"health\"] == refresh[\"health\"]` — a pure CLOSE/DRIFT_REFRESH equivalence test. Swapping the member would leave it comparing a value to itself, so **delete the `refresh` block and both equivalence assertions**, keeping the `default`/`close` arms and asserting `default[\"verdict\"] == \"stale-head\"` and `close[\"valid\"] is True`.\n- `.DRIFT_REFRESH` → `.CLOSE` at `test_plan_review_phase_validity.py:35`, `test_plan_material_pin_health_heldout.py:106`, `test_drift_refresh_candidate.py:56`.\n- New `test_plan_review_attest_drift.py::test_unresolvable_ref_reason_is_single_sourced`: the scoped and unscoped paths both yield `_unresolvable_ref_reason(ref)` verbatim.\n- New parametrized test in `test_mcp_plan_review_status.py` over all 7 `verify_signature` failure verdicts: each passes through unchanged as `verdict` and validates against the schema via `jsonschema`; plus a negative case asserting `not-closed` is now rejected.\n- Unchanged: `test_opcert_cross_environment_c21f.py:225`, `test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py` (whole file), `test_compute_validity.py:28`, `plan_review/test_94a3_material_diff.py:428`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `git grep -n \"at_current_gate_ref\\|terraform_membership_entries\\|DRIFT_REFRESH\\|_TERRAFORM_GLOB_SUFFIXES\" -- src tests docs ':!tests/fixtures'` prints nothing.\n- [ ] `git grep -c \"could not be resolved to a snapshot\" -- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py` prints `1`.\n- [ ] `python -c \"import json;e=set(json.load(open('src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_status.schema.json'))['properties']['verdict']['enum']);print('not-closed' not in e, {'mismatch','invalid','foreign_key','unavailable','unknown_kind','unknown_scheme','key_not_valid_at_era'} <= e)\"` prints `True True`.\n- [ ] `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest_gate.py` still contains `\"verdict\": result.get(\"verdict\", \"unsigned\"),` — the pass-through is retained, not suppressed.\n- [ ] `grep -c \"not-closed\" src/rebar/llm/gate_runs.py` prints `1`.\n- [ ] Both new tests are green, and `tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py` passes **unmodified**.\n- [ ] `python -m rebar.schemas.gen_types --check` is clean; `make verify` exits 0."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793396398043348757,"uuid":"ab3195f1-7a06-40f3-9797-a2432610f5a3"}